      "census_id": "W-SSC-059",
      "source_unit": "W04a",
      "frozen_source_body": "W04a writes a right-handed Minkowski Weyl equation of the form (E-sigma dot p) psi_R=0, derives the Klein-Gordon mass-shell consequence, and associates its positive- and negative-energy branches with opposite helicities. It prints the energy-momentum equation (E-sigma·p) tilde_psi_R(E,p)=0, the ordered factorization (E+sigma·p)(E-sigma·p)=E^2-|p|^2, the conditional mass shell E=±|p|, and the helicity operator (1/2)(sigma·p)/|p| with +1/2 for positive-energy particles and -1/2 for negative-energy antiparticles; these are source-written roles, not qualified lower physical laws.",
      "source_body_identity": {
        "path": "research/woit-lisi-isomorph/woit/SOURCE_SEMANTIC_CENSUS_0_70.json",
