      "census_id": "W-SSC-060",
      "source_unit": "W04a",
      "frozen_source_body": "W04a passes from the classical Weyl equation to the quantum oscillator/field description and treats Standard-Model copies, gauge-covariant derivatives, and Higgs/Yukawa mass couplings as additional matter structure rather than part of the bare spacetime representation. The source says the quantum theory is an infinite collection of complex harmonic oscillators, one for each momentum p, with annihilation and creation operators satisfying anti-commutation relations. No complete anticommutation algebra or coefficient convention is printed; do not invent one.",
