    {
      "census_id": "W-SSC-061",
      "source_unit": "W04a",
      "frozen_source_body": "W04a contrasts the right-handed Minkowski Wightman kernel with the naive Euclidean substitution and makes the failure of a one-chirality Euclidean propagator/Lagrangian a concrete Wick-rotation obstruction. The displayed source Wightman formula is tilde_W2(E,p)=(E-sigma·p)^(-1)=(E+sigma·p)/(E^2-|p|^2), while the candidate naive Schwinger continuation is tilde_S2(E,p)=(iE-sigma·p)^(-1). The second is expressly an unsuccessful conventional Wick-rotation attempt, not an established continuation; the source's conventional vector operator is a map from S_R^* to S_L and the proposed right-handed-only replacement is separate.",
